<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/qing-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Qing%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Qing Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The six-year-old Puyi abdicates, ending imperial rule in China</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/wadai-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Wadai%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Wadai Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">France abolishes the Wadai sultanate</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-nicaragua"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Nicaragua.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Nicaragua</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">US Marines land, beginning an occupation that lasts until 1933</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/argentine-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Argentine%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Argentine Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Sáenz Peña Law introduces secret and compulsory male suffrage</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sun Yat-sen becomes provisional president at Nanjing; the last Qing emperor abdicates</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/union-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Union%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Union of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The South African Native National Congress, later the ANC, is founded at Bloemfontein</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/bahai-faith"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bah%C3%A1'%C3%AD%20Faith.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bahá'í Faith</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">ʻAbdu’l-Bahá travels across North America, speaking in churches, synagogues and universities</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-cuba-1902-1959"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Cuba%20(1902-1959).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Cuba (1902-1959)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Partido Independiente de Color's attempt to set up a separate Black republic in Oriente is crushed by the army under General Monteagudo with considerable bloodshed.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/machu-picchu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Machu%20Picchu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Machu Picchu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bingham's expedition for Yale and the National Geographic Society clears and excavates the site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tibet-1912-1951"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tibet%20(1912-1951).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tibet (1912-1951)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Qing officials in Lhasa signed the Three Point Agreement for the surrender and expulsion of Qing forces from central Tibet</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/emperor-meiji"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Emperor%20Meiji.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Emperor Meiji</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The emperor dies in Tokyo and is succeeded by Yoshihito</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/sun-yat-sen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sun%20Yat-sen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sun Yat-sen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sun takes office as provisional president, then resigns in favour of Yuan Shikai</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/forbidden-city"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Forbidden%20City.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Forbidden City</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The abdication of Puyi ends its role as the political centre of China</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/thessaloniki"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Thessaloniki.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Thessaloniki</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Ottoman garrison surrenders to the Greek army</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/sanchi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sanchi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sanchi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Restoration under Sir John Marshall began and brought the structures to their present condition by 1919</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/syndicalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Syndicalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Syndicalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Italian syndicalist confederation USI is formed by veterans of the farm and factory strikes</span></li></ul></section>
